<title>AUSTRALIA: S&amp;P rates NSW T-Corp dual currency bonds AA.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P rates NSW T-Corp dual currency bonds AA.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ratings agency Standard and Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Wednesday that it had assigned its AA rating to two tranches of dual currency samurai bonds maturing October 1999 that are issued by Australia's New South Wales T-Corp.  </p>
<p>&quot;The ratings reflect the rating of its guarantor, the State of New South Wales,&quot; S&amp;P said, adding that the foreign currency outlook was positive.</p>
<p>&quot;The rating on these bonds are constrained by the AA foreign currency sovereign rating of the Commonwealth of Australia,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The two tranches total 25 billion yen, it said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
